    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this wonderful 3-bedroom / 3-bathroom semi-detached family home with a highly sought after south facing rear garden tucked away on a peaceful cul de sac in the ever-popular Elder Heath development. Elder Heath is ideally located at the foothills of the Dublin Mountains and is always in high demand as it is within easy reach of all local amenities including shopping facilities, a variety of bars & restaurants, an extensive choice of sports grounds & leisure facilities, a great mix of primary & secondary schools. The area is well serviced with excellent bus routes and road networks. The Red Luas Line is also within striking distance. \r\n\r\nBright, airy and most spacious internal living accommodation of c 110 sqm briefly comprises of entrance hallway with guest bathroom, large living room and fully fitted kitchen/dining area to the rear with separate utility/washroom. On the first floor you have three spacious bedrooms (one master ensuite) with built in wardrobes and main family bathroom, A double door from the kitchen area leads out to a private & enclosed rear garden of the lowest maintenance with artificial grass and a highly sought after south facing orientation making it perfect for relaxing on them sunny summer evenings. balcony which is benefitted by a sunny south west facing orientation making it the perfect sun trap on them long sunny summer evenings. The front offers off street parking on a peaceful cul de sac with very minimal passing traffic & lovely views of the Dublin Mountains. \r\n\r\nNo. 25 Elder Heath View comes to the market in fantastic condition throughout having been lovingly maintained by its current owners with no expense when upgrading in recent times with top quality fixtures & fittings throughout and houses of this quality don't often come to the market, there plenty additional features such as A-rated home, double-glazed windows with blinds, top quality flooring, built in wardrobes and gas fired central heating to name but a few. \r\n\r\nThis one is prime for a wide range of buyers such as 1st time buyers looking to get on the property ladder & any growing family looking to settle roots in one of Dublin 24s most sought-after developments. \r\n\r\nViewing is highly advised, please contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers for further information or to arrange viewing! \r\n\r\nAdditional Features; \r\n- BER A3\r\n- c 110 sqm \r\n- 3 Bed / 3 Bath \r\n- Semi-detached family home\r\n- Fantastic condition throughout\r\n- Tastefully decorated from top to bottom \r\n- Top quality fixtures & fittings\r\n- Entrance hallway with guest bathroom \r\n- Large living room \r\n- Fully fitted kitchen \r\n- Open plan kitchen/dining area\r\n- Separate utility/washroom \r\n- Ample storage \r\n- Carpet stairs & landing \r\n- Three generous bedrooms \r\n- Built in wardrobes \r\n- Main family bathroom \r\n- Ensuite bathroom\r\n- Maintenance free rear garden \r\n- Private & fully enclosed \r\n- Artificial grass to rear \r\n- Sunny south facing orientation \r\n- Double glazed windows \r\n- Top quality blinds \r\n- Gas fired central heating\r\n- Bright and airy home\r\n- Off street parking \r\n- Located on peaceful cul de sac \r\n- Lovely views of Dublin Mountains \r\n- Highly sought-after area \r\n- Excellent transport links \r\n- Within arm's reach of N7 and M50 Motorway \r\n- Highly sought-after development \r\n- Prime for first time buyers' & growing families \r\n- Viewing highly advised \r\n\r\nDirections: D24 Y8PN"
      },
      {
